 one of the largest  manufacturers of its kind in italy  ferruccio celebrated his success by  living a more extravagant lifestyle  champagne caviar and fast cars  he even started to collect jaguars  mercedes maseratis and ferraris but none  of them completely satisfied him he was  particularly disappointed with his  ferrari 250 gt since the clutch would  always break down  one day he brought his ferrari down to  the mechanic for repairs  he then found out that the clutch was  identical to the one fitted onto one of  his tractors this didn't sit well with  him since he paid 10 euros for the  clutch his tractor used and paid ferrari  1 000 euros for the same part later he  decided to tell enzo ferrari the founder  of ferrari about the imperfections he  found in his car along with the clutches  needing frequent repairs they were  considered too noisy and rough on the  road  ferruccio was just trying to give advice  to enzo on how to improve his car so it  would drive better but enzo simply said  you're a tractor driver you're a farmer  you shouldn't complain about my cars  because they're the best cars in the  world  that infuriated ferruccio and he was  determined to prove enzo wrong  many called his conquest crazy and  thought he'd waste his fortune still he  went ahead and started a new company  under his own name  he hired three of ferrari's ex-employees  and bought a large plot of land to build  a factory  in just nine months he completed his  first sports car featuring his  astrological sign as the emblem the  lamborghini 350 gt was born it was  considered a technical masterpiece and  included a v12 engine five-speed  transmission four-wheel disc brakes and  four-wheel independent suspension  it was unveiled for the first time at  the turin motor show and praised by  customers and critics his first car was  described as sophisticated and classy it  was also easy to drive  he proved to enzo and his doubters that  he wasn't just a farmer but also a  mechanical genius capable of building  superior cars  over the next few years his tractor and  sports car business flourished his  leadership style led to his team  building the 400 gt and a secret project  the miura p400 it was developed as a  street race car and was the first car in  history to be made with a rear mid  engine layout  the development of the mural was  actually kept a secret from ferruccio  since he wasn't a big fan of street race  cars as he'd been involved in a crash  before  when ferruccio found out he decided not  to scrap the idea it turned out to be  one of the best decisions he ever made  the miura became known as the world's  first supercar and its rear mid-engine  layout became the standard for all high  performance cars from then on  lamborghini continued its successful  streak and debuted more celebrated  models such as the espada the aslero the  hamara the uruko and the kuntash they  were said to be superior to other sports  cars since they didn't use anyone else's  parts and the countach was said to be  the most written about car in history  unfortunately his success came to a halt  after facing a series of events beyond  his control a deal to supply bolivia  with 5 000 tractors was cancelled after  the country faced a coup the loss forced  him to sell his tractor company and 51  percent of his lamborghini shares the  global stock market experienced a  dramatic crash and opec started an oil  embargo it led to increased fuel prices  and threw the automotive industry into  turmoil ferruccio did his best to keep  his business alive and managed to find  buyers for his unsold tractors still he  decided to retire early and sold the  remaining 49 of his lamborghini shares  but he did keep a heating company that  he owned and gave it to his son tonino  later tonino pivoted towards building a  successful fashion and luxury business  under the family name  meanwhile the new owners of lamborghini  tried to revive its brand but failed  afterwards the company was 